  <para style="h">Malakai</para>
  <para style="toc1">Malakai</para>
  <para style="toc2">Malakai</para>
  <para style="toc3">Mal</para>
  <para style="mt1">Malakai</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="MAL 1" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="MAL 1:1" />Prọfesi a-atooho Abọọñ e-enọọhọ esọk Isrel a-aboiyoke ke inua Malakai.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:1 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Malakai </char><char style="ft" closed="false">awuọñọ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">isʌñutom mmi.</char></note><verse eid="MAL 1:1" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Isrel Ayịk Ima Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="MAL 1:2" />“Ami mmima ndufo,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 1:2">“Ado ndufo e-ebịp, ‘Afo ima ñnyịn die?’</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 1:2">“Nte Isọ ikidooho ayịneka Yekọb?” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ. “Ado ami mmema Yekọb, <verse eid="MAL 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MAL 1:3" />ado mmesua Isọ, ami mmenyʌñ ñkappa abio anyọñ abod amọ nnam anye aforo mbiara isọñ, ñnyʌñ nsaana udeeme amọ nnọ mme ewaikọd ake akpautatan.”<verse eid="MAL 1:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="MAL 1:4" />Edọm akeme adibo, “Akpesʌkado emaikan ñnyịn, ñnyịn iyaimaana ibọp ñwuudo abio ñnyịn.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 1:4">Ado se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ ado ami: “Ammọ ekeme adibọp, ado ami ñyaawuut. Eyaekoot ammọ Isọñ Ibak, mbon e-ebaaha ke idak iyadesịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> afịd ini. <verse eid="MAL 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MAL 1:5" />Afo ayaakịt anye ke anyen mfo anyʌñ abo, ‘<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado akpọsọñ ke Isrel ye ke mme idʌñ e-ewuọhọ ekpọñ mme adaña amọ!’<verse eid="MAL 1:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ubiat Edioomo ke Mme Anieñe Ndo Uwa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="MAL 1:6" />“Ayịn awodeen akpono ete amọ, afʌn ñko akpono eteufọk amọ. Adieke ami ndooho ete, mmọ ukpono a-adotto ye ami? Adieke ami ndooho eteufọk, mmọ ukpono a-adotto ye ami?” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 1:6">“Ado ndufo mme aku i-inọọhọ anyịñ mmi ukpono.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 1:6">“Ado ndufo ebịp, ‘Ñnyịn inam die imiinọọhọ anyịñ mfo ukpono?’<verse eid="MAL 1:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="MAL 1:7" />“Ke adinọ ndidia se emaesappa ke akpokoro uwa mmi.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 1:7">“Ado ndufo ebịp, ‘Ñnyịn inam die usappa fiin?’</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 1:7">“Ke adibo ke akpokoro <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> idotto ukpono. <verse eid="MAL 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MAL 1:8" />Ke ini ndufo enọọhọ mme unam e-edooho nnan nte ñkpọ uwa, nte ado idiọọhọ? Ke ini ndufo ekamake unam se ido mbʌñọ me unam se inie udọñọ enam uwa, nte ado idiọọhọ? Idomo adikama ammọ nnọọ adaukara ndufo! Nte anye ayaanem esịd ye ndufo? Nte anye ayaibọ ndufo?” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.<verse eid="MAL 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="MAL 1:9" />“Idahami kpe Abasi ubọk nọ anye anie mbọm ibaña ñnyịn. Ye utọ mme enọ ado ke ubọk ndufo, nte anye ayaibọ ndufo?” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.<verse eid="MAL 1:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="MAL 1:10" />“Sai, die ke keed ke atu ndufo akpebet mme udọk tembịd, mbaak ndufo ididomo mme ikpu-ikpu ikañ ke akpokoro uwa mmi! Ami nnemme esịd ye ndufo,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ, “ami ñko ndiibọọhọ enọ ndomokeed nto ubọk ndufo. <verse eid="MAL 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MAL 1:11" />Anyịñ mmi ayaakpon ke atu mme idịd, tọọñọ ke itie nte utịn asakka tutu asịm itie nte utịn asop. Ke afịd itie eyaeben insensi ye nti ndisana enọ ensọk miin, sia anyịñ mmi ayaakpon ke atu mme idịd,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.<verse eid="MAL 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="MAL 1:12" />“Ado ndufo emesịn anyịñ mmi ke ndek ke adibo, ‘Emesappa akpokoro Abọọñ,’ ñko, ‘Ndidia amọ ado mbubiam.’ <verse eid="MAL 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MAL 1:13" />Ndin ndufo ete, ‘Nsoo utọ mbiomo!’ ndufo enyʌñ enuuno anye emiom-emiom,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 1:13">“Ndufo emaeben mme unam se inie unọmọ, unam se ido mbʌñọ ye unam se inie udọñọ enọ nte mme ñkpọ uwa, nte a-ado se ami ñkpebọọ ammọ nto ubọk ndufo?” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ. <verse eid="MAL 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MAL 1:14" />“Adọdiọọk anọ awo utʌk a-anieghe ayaara unam ke atu mme ufene amọ anyʌñ anwọñọ adinọ anye, ado akema anye akama unam a-anieghe ndo anam uwa anọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Sia ami ndo ekamba adidem,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ, “ndin ana ebaak anyịñ mmi ke atu mme idịd.<verse eid="MAL 1:14" /></para>
  <chapter eid="MAL 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="MAL 2" />
  <para style="s1">Etịmme Edʌt Mme Aku Abasi Utọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="MAL 2:1" />“Idahami ndin, ndufo mme aku Abasi, ndʌdutọñ ami inie ndufo. <verse eid="MAL 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MAL 2:2" />Adieke ndufo imiikpañña utọñ, ñko adieke ndufo imiibiereke adikpono anyịñ mmi,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ, “ami ñyaadọñ isuuñọ inọ ndufo, ami ñyaanyʌñ nsuuñọ mme adidiọñ ndufo. Ii, ami mmesosuuñọ ammọ, sia ndufo imiibiereke adiñkpono miin.<verse eid="MAL 2:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="MAL 2:3" />“Ke ntak ndufo ami ñyaasua nnọ ubon ndufo, ami ñyaikpenne ndufo uduañ a-atooho mme unam uwa usọrọ ndufo ke iso, ndin eyaiben ndufo esio ye anye. <verse eid="MAL 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MAL 2:4" />Ndufo eyaenyʌñ ediọọñọ ke ami ñkedọñ mme idiọọñọ ami inọọ ndufo nọ ato do edioomo mmi ye Lifai aka iso,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ. <verse eid="MAL 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MAL 2:5" />“Edioomo mmi akedo ye anye, edioomo uwem ye emem, ami mmaanyʌñ nnọ anye uwem ye emem; akena anye añkpono miin, ndin anye amaanyʌñ añkpono miin anyʌñ ateeñe anyịñ mmi. <verse eid="MAL 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MAL 2:6" />Item akpanikọ amaaba ke inua amọ ndin awo ikikịtte nsu ndomokeed ke ñkpọkinua amọ. Anye amaasaña ye ami ke emem ye adinen ido, anyʌñ awọññọ uwak awo akpọñ uwem idiọọkñkpọ.<verse eid="MAL 2:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="MAL 2:7" />“Aku Abasi akpena anie ifiọk, sia anye ado isʌñutom <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan, ndin mme awo eyem item uwem eto inua amọ. <verse eid="MAL 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MAL 2:8" />Ado afo amewọññọ akpọñ usʌñ ndin ato ke ukpeebñkpọ mfo amenam uwak awo eduọ; afo amebiat edioomo ye Lifai,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ. <verse eid="MAL 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MAL 2:9" />“Ke ntoro ami mmenam nọ afo ado ñkpọ ndọk ye asuenne ke iso mbon awo, sia afo ukeeneke mme usʌñ mmi ado anam ñkpọ anyen awo ke mme ñkpọ e-ebañake mbed.”<verse eid="MAL 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Udiañña Ndọ ado Ubiat Edioomo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="MAL 2:10" />Nte afịd ñnyịn inieghe Ete keed? Nte idooho Abasi keed akibot ñnyịn? Nsoo inam nọ ñnyịn isappa edioomo mme eteete ñnyịn ke aditre adinam akpanikọ nnọọ emọ-emọ?<verse eid="MAL 2:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="MAL 2:11" />Yuda a-atre adinam akpanikọ. E-enam ataa mbubiam ñkpọ ke Isrel ye ke Yeruselem: Yuda asappa adisana itie <char style="nd">A-Abọọñ</char> amaaha ke adidọ ibaan e-ekponoke asen abasi. <verse eid="MAL 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MAL 2:12" />Amaado awodeen se inam ñkpọ ami, akee awo anye akpedodo, yak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> asio anye afep ke mme atayad Yekọb, akpesʌkado a-anye abenne enọ asọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan.<verse eid="MAL 2:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="MAL 2:13" />Ñkpọ mfen se afo anam: Afo ameyọhọ akpokoro uwa <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ye mmọọñayịd. Afo ametua anyʌñ afoho sia anye iseeghe mme enọ mfo aba ye mfọn, inyʌññọ ima adibọ ammọ ke idadesịd nto ubọk mfo. <verse eid="MAL 2:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MAL 2:14" />Afo amebịp abo, “Ntaha?” Ntak ado ke <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ado ntiense ke ufọọd mfo ye anwaan uyịn mfo. Afo unamma akpanikọ ye anye, akpesʌkado a-anye adooho nsaña mfo, anwaan ndọ edioomo mfo.<verse eid="MAL 2:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="MAL 2:15" />Nte idooho Abasi keed akibot ndufo? Abasi inie ndufo ke abʌkidem ye ke sịbidịd. Ndin nsoo ke Abasi keed ami ayem? Enọ asañake ye mbaak Abasi. Ke ntoro kpeme idem, kuunyʌñ utre adinam akpanikọ nnọọ anwaan uyịn mfo.<verse eid="MAL 2:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="MAL 2:16" />“Awo se isua inyʌñ isio anwaan amọ ke ndọ,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, Abasi Isrel atañ, “a-anam afai ye anye a-anye akpekpemeke,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 2:16">Ke ntoro kpeme idem, kuunyʌñ utre adinam akpanikọ nnọọ anwaan uyịn mfo.<verse eid="MAL 2:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ubiat Edioomo ke Ukwañ Ikpe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="MAL 2:17" />Ndufo emenam esịd abʌññọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke ntak mme ikọ ndufo.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 2:17">Ndufo emebịp “Die ke ñnyịn inam esịd abʌññọ anye?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 2:17">Ke adibo, “Afịd mbon se inam ndiọiñkpọ e-efọọn ke anyen <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, anye ñko a-anem esịd ye ammọ” me ke adibo “Mmọ anye Abasi a-adooho akpe unen?”<verse eid="MAL 2:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="MAL 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="MAL 3" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="MAL 3:1" />“Ami ñyaadọñ isʌñutom mmi, anye ayaadiọñ usʌñ anịm annọ miin. Ndin ke adiwad ini <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> a-afo ayemmeyem ayaadidʌk tembịd amọ; ndin isʌñutom edioomo a-afo anieghe udọñ abaña, ayaadi,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.<verse eid="MAL 3:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="MAL 3:2" />Ado anie adiikan ida ke usen adidi amọ? Anie akeme adida ke ini anye abiọññọke? Sia anye adiiba nte ikañ anamusọ me nte atọñ ayedafọñ. <verse eid="MAL 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MAL 3:3" />Anye adiitie nte andinam asana ye andidiọñ silfa; anye ayaanam mbon Lifai esana anyʌñ adiọñ ammọ nte kold ye silfa. Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaanie mme awo se idiiben enọ idi ke adinenido, <verse eid="MAL 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MAL 3:4" />ñko <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaabọ mme enọ Yuda ye Yeruselem, nte mme usen e-ekeboiyoke, nte mme ñkaan isua.<verse eid="MAL 3:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="MAL 3:5" />“Ke ntoro ami ñyaatọọñọ ikpe ye afo. Ami ñyaasọsọp adinọ ikọ ntiense mbaña mme mbiamfa, mme asịn efịbe ye mme ntiense nsu, mbaña mbon e-ebọọhọ mme anamutom akʌkutom ammọ ke ñwo, mbaña mbon e-efiighe mme ebekpa ye nditọakpa, e-enyʌññọ ebiọọñọ mme isenawo ke atu ndufo unenikpe, ado imfegheke miin anyen,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.<verse eid="MAL 3:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adikpe Ayọhọ Mbaak Keed ke Itie Duob</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="MAL 3:6" />“Ami <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ñkpuhoke. Ke ntoro ndufo ubon Yekọb ikịtte nsobo. <verse eid="MAL 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MAL 3:7" />Atọọñọ ke ini mme eteete ndufo, ndufo emaekanna ekpọñ mme ewʌhọ mmi, inyʌññọ inịm ammọ. Itịmme iñkeene miin, ami ñko ñyaatịmme ikeene ndufo,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 3:7">“Ado ndufo ebịp, ‘Die ke ñnyịn idiitịmme ubịne?’<verse eid="MAL 3:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="MAL 3:8" />“Nte ñkaña awo akeme aditʌk Abasi? Ado ndufo ementʌk miin.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 3:8">“Ado ndufo ebịp, ‘Die ke ñnyịn utʌk fiin?’</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 3:8">“Ke ayọhọ mbaak keed ke itie duob ye mme enọ. <verse eid="MAL 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MAL 3:9" />Ndufo eba ke idak isuuñọ, afịd idịd ndufo, sia ndufo ementʌk miin. <verse eid="MAL 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MAL 3:10" />Iben afịd ayọhọ mbaak keed ke itie duob idi ke ufọk ubonoñkpọ, nọ ndidia aba ke ufọk mmi. Ikama ami indomo miin ise,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ, “me ami ndiibeereke mme inuaatob anyọñ ñnyʌñ ñnwañña uwak adidiọñ inọ ndufo tutu ufañ ibaaha aba. <verse eid="MAL 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MAL 3:11" />Ami ñyaakpan ndiọi unam adibiat mme ñkpọ inwañ ndufo, ndin mme fain ke inwañ ndufo idiibekkeke mbemiso anye adat,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ. <verse eid="MAL 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MAL 3:12" />“Ndin afịd mme idịd eyaukoot fiin adisana, sia isọñ mfo adiido isọñ inemesịd,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.<verse eid="MAL 3:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Isrel Etañ Ikọ ye Abasi ke Ñkokkoidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="MAL 3:13" />“Ndufo emetañ ikọ ke ñkokkoidem ye ami,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="MAL 3:13">“Ado ndufo ebịp, ‘Nsoo ke ñnyịn itañ udian fiin?’<verse eid="MAL 3:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="MAL 3:14" />“Ndufo emebo, ‘Ufọn ibaaha adinam ñkpọ nnọọ Abasi. Nsoo udod ke ñnyịn idia ito adinam se anye ayem ndin isaña nte mbon e-etieghe ikpo ke iso <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan? <verse eid="MAL 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MAL 3:15" />Ado idahami ñnyịn ikoot mbon ñkokkoidem mbon se emaekediọñ. Ke akpanikọ mme anam idiọọkñkpọ eforo, ndin idem ini se ammọ edomo Abasi ese, ñkpọ ndomokeed inamma ammọ.’ ”<verse eid="MAL 3:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñyọhọnsʌhọ Mme Anam Akpanikọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="MAL 3:16" />Akem mbon se ibaak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> emaetañ ikọ ye emọ-emọ, ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaakpañ utọñ anyʌñ akop. Emaewet ñwed ke iso amọ aditoiyo mbaña mbon se ikibaak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> inyʌñ ikpono anyịñ amọ.<verse eid="MAL 3:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="MAL 3:17" />“Ke usen se ami ndiisio ñkpọ nnam,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ, “ammọ eyaedo ñkpọuto udeeme mmi. Ami ñyaafak ammọ, kpa naña ete anie mbọm abaña anyʌñ afak ayịn a-anamma ñkpọ anọ anye. <verse eid="MAL 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MAL 3:18" />Ndin afo ayaamaana akịt ukpʌhọde a-abaaha ke ufọọd ndinen awo ye mbon ibak, ke ufọọd mbon se inam ñkpọ inọ Abasi ye mbon se imiinamma ñkpọ inọ anye.<verse eid="MAL 3:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="MAL 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="MAL 4" />
  <para style="s1">Ikpe ye Adimaana Ndemme Akaaña</para>
  <para style="p">
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">4: </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke mme ikpañwed Hibru ewet Mal 4:1-6 nte Mal 3:19-24.</char>
    </note> <verse number="1" style="v" sid="MAL 4:1" />“Ke akpanikọ usen ado asʌk adi; anye adiisak nte ñkpọdiọhọ ikañ. Afịd mbon ntañidem ye mme anam idiọọk ediido ikpitok, ndin usen a-adiighe ke iso ammọ eyaesịn ammọ ke ikañ,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ. “Adʌñ me ñkọk ndomokeed idiisʌhọke inọ ammọ. <verse eid="MAL 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MAL 4:2" />Amaado ndufo e-ekponoke anyịñ mmi, utịn adinenido asañake ye ukọk ayaasakka inọ ndufo. Ndufo eyaewuọ enyʌñ edia uwem nte mme ñyịn enañ e-enọọhọ nti ndidia. <verse eid="MAL 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MAL 4:3" />Ndin ndufo eyaesọnnọ mbon ibak; ammọ eyaekappa edo ntọñ ke esịd ekaikpad ndufo ke usen a-ami ndiitịppe ñkpọ nnam,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.<verse eid="MAL 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="MAL 4:4" />“Toiyo mbed isʌñutom mmi Moses, mme ewʌhọ ye mme mbed a-ami ñkenọọhọ esọk afịd nditọ Isrel ke Họreb.<verse eid="MAL 4:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="MAL 4:5" />“Se, ami ñyaadọñ prọfed Elaiya nnọ isọk ndufo mbemiso ekamba usen ndịk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> adi. <verse eid="MAL 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MAL 4:6" />Anye ayaawọññọ esịd mme ete ye mme eka anọ nditọ ammọ, anyʌñ awọññọ esịd nditọ anọ mme ete ye mme eka ammọ; imiidooho ntoro ami ñyaadi ndisobo isọñ ataa afịd-afịd.”<verse eid="MAL 4:6" /></para>
  <chapter eid="MAL 4" />
</usx>